    "notes": "OSM way 458510977 identifies the crossing. Exact RN16 centerline joins place the Chaco approach and the curved Corrientes landing. Two short native sidewalk tails remain on the Chaco approach and no native deck or path is rendered over the channel. The authored 2.24 km crossing follows the full PMTiles RN16 bridge and approach alignment. Published bridge-length conventions exclude different portions of the mapped landings. Tower locations, approach pier spacing, deck grades and fender forms are reconstructed from exterior photographs and standard viewer terrain. The center span uses the recorded 245 m length. The bridge does not encode surveyed structural dimensions or hydraulic clearance. The current viewer river and riverbanks are retained. The amount of exposed pier and fender above water varies with host water levels."
  },
